# Game Performance Overlay & Telemetry (`game-performance-overlay-telemetry`)

The `game-performance-overlay-telemetry` skill provides tools and configuration recipes for deploying live in-game telemetry across Linux (Vulkan / OpenGL / Wine / Proton) and Windows game engines without conflicting with in-game minimaps, crosshairs, or UI menus.

---

## 1. Core Telemetry Metrics

To accurately evaluate performance bottlenecks (GPU vs CPU bound, VRAM starvation, thermal throttling), an effective HUD must track:

| Metric | Target / Purpose | Diagnostic Insight |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **FPS & Frametime Graph** | Real-time frame latency (ms) | Spikes indicate asset streaming stutters, shader compilation stalls, or garbage collection. |
| **1% & 0.1% Lows** | Micro-stutter measurement | A stable 60 FPS with 25 FPS 1% lows feels choppy and indicates frame pacing defects. |
| **GPU Usage & VRAM Allocation** | Capacity & bus saturation | If VRAM approaches 95%+ of 8GB, textures thrash over PCIe bus, causing severe frame drops. |
| **CPU Usage, Frequency & Power** | Thread core utilization & watts | Low GPU usage + high single-core frequency points to main-thread draw call bottlenecks. |
| **Thermals (°C)** | Core & hotspot temperatures | Temperatures exceeding 85°C trigger thermal downclocking and sudden framerate degradation. |

---

## 2. MangoHud Configuration for Wine / Proton

MangoHud is the standard Linux gaming overlay. By default, it docks in `top-left`, colliding directly with S.T.A.L.K.E.R. and RPG minimaps. Setting `position=top-right` ensures clean visibility.

### A. Recommended Telemetry Profile (`top-right`)
File: `~/.config/MangoHud/MangoHud.conf` (or per-app `~/.config/MangoHud/xr_3da.conf`):

```ini
legacy_layout=false
gpu_stats=true
gpu_temp=true
gpu_core_clock=true
gpu_mem_clock=true
gpu_power=true
gpu_text=GPU

cpu_stats=true
cpu_temp=true
cpu_power=true
cpu_mhz=true
cpu_text=CPU

vram=true
ram=true
fps=true
fps_sampling_period=500
frametime=true
frame_timing=1

hud_no_margin=true
table_columns=3
font_size=20
position=top-right
background_alpha=0.4
round_corners=6

toggle_hud=Shift_R+F12
toggle_logging=Shift_L+F2
```

### B. Launching Games with MangoHud
```bash
# Direct executable launch:
mangohud wine bin/x64/xrEngine.exe

# Steam Proton launch option:
mangohud %command%

# Gamescope + MangoHud:
gamescope -W 1920 -H 1080 -b --mangoapp -- wine bin/x64/xrEngine.exe
```

